{
 "version": 1,
 "title": "Advanced 8 \u00b7 Rhythm from envelopes",
 "text": "An envelope normally runs once per key. Its RETRIG input starts it again while the key is still held: plug a Clock into it and a held chord becomes a rhythm, the trance gate. The VCA's envelope here has no sustain, so each retrigger is a short pulse, sixteen to the bar. A second envelope on the filter is retriggered on the eighths: the brightness pulses at half the speed, against the volume. Hold a chord.\n\nTry: the volume envelope's DECAY (long: the pulses blur into a pad); move its RETRIG cable to 1/8 or BEAT; the filter envelope on BAR (one sweep per bar); give the volume envelope some SUSTAIN (it pulses on top of a held level instead of from silence); TEMPO.",
